WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:04.366
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:04.366 --> 00:00:06.853
Today we're going to talk
about how you can live life

00:00:06.853 --> 00:00:08.559
without regrets.

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:10.315
As always guys as you're
watching the clips,

00:00:10.315 --> 00:00:12.119
if you hear somebody say something

00:00:12.119 --> 00:00:13.696
that really resonates with you,

00:00:13.696 --> 00:00:15.223
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:16.654
and put quotes around it so other people

00:00:16.654 --> 00:00:18.117
can be inspired as well.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.645
Also when you write it down,

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:22.847
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself too.

00:00:22.847 --> 00:00:23.854
Enjoy.

00:00:23.854 --> 00:00:27.187
(gentle cheerful music)

00:00:41.913 --> 00:00:44.996
- The biggest poison in us is regret.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.211
It's poison.

00:00:49.211 --> 00:00:53.378
And I push so hard, so hard,
and will through my vehicle,

00:00:54.591 --> 00:00:58.557
which isn't meditation, which
isn't health and wellness,

00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:00.149
which isn't non-profit.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:03.108
My people's business, I can't help it.

00:01:03.108 --> 00:01:04.197
It's what I love.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.030
I love building businesses.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.317
I love competing with
you, I want to beat you.

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:08.796
I love that game.

00:01:08.796 --> 00:01:11.917
But through that vehicle,
I will always push

00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:13.835
a lack of regret.

00:01:13.835 --> 00:01:16.045
And awareness to how good it really is.

00:01:16.045 --> 00:01:18.288
You're more than welcome
to me about how bad it is

00:01:18.288 --> 00:01:23.246
or why you can't because or
what, but it's just not true.

00:01:23.246 --> 00:01:27.730
Because if anybody ever
did it, then you can too.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.186
Stop making excuses.

00:01:30.186 --> 00:01:32.071
Stop complaining.

00:01:32.071 --> 00:01:33.843
Nobody's listening.

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:36.102
They may pretend they're listening,

00:01:36.102 --> 00:01:38.476
the market doesn't care.

00:01:38.476 --> 00:01:41.954
What you need to do is
make one person happy, you.

00:01:41.954 --> 00:01:44.116
Then you can make everybody else happy.

00:01:44.116 --> 00:01:46.050
You know why I like making people happy?

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.633
'Cause I'm already happy.

00:01:47.633 --> 00:01:51.755
And so I implore you to
take this last little rant

00:01:51.755 --> 00:01:54.404
and really look at your
face and understand

00:01:54.404 --> 00:01:56.290
are you doing the things that are putting

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.630
you in a position to succeed?

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.711
Not just in the business
world, but in life.

00:02:00.711 --> 00:02:01.849
Because it's super important

00:02:01.849 --> 00:02:04.189
because boy, when you're happy in life,

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:06.106
your business can roll.

00:02:10.268 --> 00:02:12.365
- We walk around thinking
people look at us

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.576
as the star in our movie, but they don't.

00:02:14.576 --> 00:02:16.672
Everybody else is living the same dream.

00:02:16.672 --> 00:02:19.566
They're walking around the
star of their own movie.

00:02:19.566 --> 00:02:21.597
And we're just a film
extra in their movie.

00:02:21.597 --> 00:02:24.474
So if we stop and taking the actions

00:02:24.474 --> 00:02:26.636
that we think will lead towards success,

00:02:26.636 --> 00:02:28.310
because we think we're worried about

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.846
what the good opinion of
other people will do to us,

00:02:30.846 --> 00:02:33.690
I got news for you, so listen carefully.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.283
I don't get on my soapbox
about many things,

00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:38.565
but I'm getting on it about this guys.

00:02:38.565 --> 00:02:42.110
Nobody cares enough about you
to bother to give an opinion

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:43.768
because they're too
busy being worried about

00:02:43.768 --> 00:02:46.156
what they think you're thinking of them.

00:02:46.156 --> 00:02:49.310
Failure, failure is not taking the step.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.658
Failure is not picking up the bat

00:02:50.658 --> 00:02:52.251
and swinging it at life.

00:02:52.251 --> 00:02:55.274
Failure is getting to the end of this game

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:57.615
and regretting what we didn't do.

00:02:57.615 --> 00:03:00.427
Failure is about saying what if.

00:03:00.427 --> 00:03:02.556
Failure is lying on
your death bed thinking,

00:03:02.556 --> 00:03:06.652
oh well if I only I could go
back and do fill in the blank.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:07.725
You know something?

00:03:07.725 --> 00:03:09.886
To me, failure isn't falling down.

00:03:09.886 --> 00:03:11.430
It's staying down when you've fallen.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.136
You have to fail by the
definition of oh I didn't succeed

00:03:15.136 --> 00:03:17.526
in order so you can succeed.

00:03:17.526 --> 00:03:19.135
That's what life is about.

00:03:19.135 --> 00:03:20.874
It's not about taking it with at the end,

00:03:20.874 --> 00:03:22.499
it's not about score keeping.

00:03:22.499 --> 00:03:24.970
I've probably failed
more times than I've won.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.099
But I keep my average
number of tries high.

00:03:27.099 --> 00:03:28.513
And do you know what happens?

00:03:28.513 --> 00:03:29.375
Guess what?

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:33.146
You tap into the lesson of
history that most people ignore.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.421
And that is this, it's
the paradox of history.

00:03:35.421 --> 00:03:37.746
That those that will
risk the least in life

00:03:37.746 --> 00:03:41.045
usually end up with the least in life.

00:03:41.045 --> 00:03:42.703
Just because our brain won't tell us that

00:03:42.703 --> 00:03:44.621
when we have to pay
our mortgage on Friday,

00:03:44.621 --> 00:03:46.377
doesn't mean it isn't true.

00:03:46.377 --> 00:03:48.457
So get up and get in the game.

00:03:48.457 --> 00:03:50.456
Who you are right now watching this

00:03:50.456 --> 00:03:53.236
is as a result of your
failures not your successes.

00:03:53.236 --> 00:03:54.747
It is when we're tested.

00:03:54.747 --> 00:03:57.494
When the storm is ripping
the branches off our tree.

00:03:57.494 --> 00:04:00.274
And when the rain clouds are there

00:04:00.274 --> 00:04:01.525
and we think we've got nothing left.

00:04:01.525 --> 00:04:03.492
That's who we are at our best,

00:04:03.492 --> 00:04:05.589
when we show up when we're tested.

00:04:05.589 --> 00:04:07.913
The strongest trees grow
in the strongest winds.

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.994
Not in the best soil.

00:04:09.994 --> 00:04:11.863
So next time you have an opportunity,

00:04:11.863 --> 00:04:13.781
next time you start to question

00:04:13.781 --> 00:04:15.715
whether you should step forward or not,

00:04:15.715 --> 00:04:17.788
will it be a white
square on the chessboard

00:04:17.788 --> 00:04:18.867
or a dark square, who care?

00:04:18.867 --> 00:04:20.282
Get in the game.

00:04:20.282 --> 00:04:21.598
Swing the bat.

00:04:21.598 --> 00:04:22.752
Be all you can be.

00:04:22.752 --> 00:04:24.833
Get up and if anybody
says, oh you're doing that,

00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:27.319
or oh you did that, oh look
it you failed, know this.

00:04:27.319 --> 00:04:31.058
They're failing in their judgment of you.

00:04:31.058 --> 00:04:34.227
Not in your ability to pick
up the bat and swing it again.

00:04:34.227 --> 00:04:36.519
That's the person you were
born to be my friends.

00:04:36.519 --> 00:04:38.226
Alright, that's the person who you are.

00:04:38.226 --> 00:04:40.274
You were born a miracle,
you are good enough.

00:04:40.274 --> 00:04:42.826
You don't need me to tell
you that, you already are.

00:04:42.826 --> 00:04:45.329
Get out there, get in
the game, go embrace it,

00:04:45.329 --> 00:04:48.515
and if you fall over, pick
yourself up, swing the bat again,

00:04:48.515 --> 00:04:50.676
and let's go play this game of life.

00:04:50.676 --> 00:04:53.009
- When I decided to do this,

00:04:54.025 --> 00:04:57.698
I first talked to my
wife who is sitting here

00:04:57.698 --> 00:04:58.901
in the audience.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:03.452
And she had married a
relatively stable, goofy,

00:05:03.452 --> 00:05:05.906
but still relatively stable person

00:05:05.906 --> 00:05:08.003
working at a Wall Street firm.

00:05:08.003 --> 00:05:10.084
I worked at a quantitative hedge fund.

00:05:10.084 --> 00:05:12.213
And this was a hard decision.

00:05:12.213 --> 00:05:15.480
And I was looking for the right framework

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.568
in which to make that kind
of important decision.

00:05:18.568 --> 00:05:21.591
And the right framework I found

00:05:21.591 --> 00:05:24.663
is a regret minimization framework.

00:05:24.663 --> 00:05:28.223
And that's just a nerdy way
of saying that you want to

00:05:28.223 --> 00:05:31.068
project yourself to age 80.

00:05:31.068 --> 00:05:33.489
And then think back over your life.

00:05:33.489 --> 00:05:37.537
And if you're 80, you want to
minimize the number of regrets

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.065
you have throughout that period of time.

00:05:39.065 --> 00:05:41.568
I think this is something
a lot of people do.

00:05:41.568 --> 00:05:45.729
Maybe subconsciously,
very few people probably

00:05:45.729 --> 00:05:47.629
name it regret minimization framework,

00:05:47.629 --> 00:05:50.263
because most people are
healthier than that.

00:05:50.263 --> 00:05:53.846
But it was a very clear
way for me to think

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.594
about making that kind of life decision.

00:05:57.594 --> 00:06:01.901
And the way it helped was I thought, okay.

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:04.372
If I go do this thing and
participate in this thing

00:06:04.372 --> 00:06:06.257
called the internet,
that I genuinely believe

00:06:06.257 --> 00:06:09.703
is going to be a big deal, and if I fail,

00:06:09.703 --> 00:06:11.784
am I going to regret
having tried and failed?

00:06:11.784 --> 00:06:14.076
I knew the answer to that was no.

00:06:14.076 --> 00:06:17.159
But I also knew that if I didn't try,

00:06:19.082 --> 00:06:20.837
that I would always regret that.

00:06:20.837 --> 00:06:22.885
I would always wonder
and it would haunt me

00:06:22.885 --> 00:06:24.885
until that mythical day.

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:28.720
- One of the greatest problems in life

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.630
is that we don't forgive
ourselves for the mistakes

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:33.206
that we've made.

00:06:33.206 --> 00:06:37.904
We carry them around and we
beat ourselves up about them.

00:06:37.904 --> 00:06:39.432
But understand this.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:42.109
The person who did those
things in your past

00:06:42.109 --> 00:06:45.755
is not the same person that you are today.

00:06:45.755 --> 00:06:48.631
In fact, you are a
completely different person

00:06:48.631 --> 00:06:51.671
with different experiences
and different knowledge

00:06:51.671 --> 00:06:54.548
and different wisdom
and different insights.

00:06:54.548 --> 00:06:56.921
The person who did those
things that you still regret

00:06:56.921 --> 00:06:58.254
is not you.

00:06:58.254 --> 00:07:01.342
It was a younger version of yourself.

00:07:01.342 --> 00:07:04.057
Almost like another person altogether.

00:07:04.057 --> 00:07:07.242
So let yourself off the hook.

00:07:07.242 --> 00:07:10.558
It's alright, everyone makes mistakes.

00:07:10.558 --> 00:07:13.565
- Whatever's happened
has happened I'm afraid.

00:07:13.565 --> 00:07:14.492
Deal with it.

00:07:14.492 --> 00:07:16.523
I don't want to deal with it Ralph.

00:07:16.523 --> 00:07:18.945
That was me on my early journey.

00:07:18.945 --> 00:07:22.112
I have worked in a lot of shoddy jobs.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:27.537
And for a long time, I
was preventing myself

00:07:28.519 --> 00:07:30.177
from becoming my greatest version,

00:07:30.177 --> 00:07:32.387
hanging around with people,

00:07:32.387 --> 00:07:36.054
not living a lifestyle
I'm living right now.

00:07:37.393 --> 00:07:40.893
But if I think back and say, gosh actually

00:07:43.505 --> 00:07:45.569
I shouldn't have done that.

00:07:45.569 --> 00:07:47.325
I could've done that.

00:07:47.325 --> 00:07:49.075
I would've done this.

00:07:50.315 --> 00:07:52.148
What does that change?

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:56.687
You see we often think that if
we think longer on a problem,

00:07:56.687 --> 00:07:57.678
it's going to change it,

00:07:57.678 --> 00:08:00.458
but thinking doesn't
actually change things.

00:08:00.458 --> 00:08:01.953
Only radical action.

00:08:01.953 --> 00:08:04.697
So what's helped me along
my journey is to say

00:08:04.697 --> 00:08:05.614
okay, yeah.

00:08:07.137 --> 00:08:09.804
A lot of my past isn't the best,

00:08:11.363 --> 00:08:12.778
but a lot of it is.

00:08:12.778 --> 00:08:15.541
You see it's always a
matter of what you focus on

00:08:15.541 --> 00:08:18.011
when dealing with the past.

00:08:18.011 --> 00:08:20.970
It's that emotion that's like

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.470
can I get a hello?

00:08:26.756 --> 00:08:29.089
A lot of us we only focus on

00:08:31.291 --> 00:08:34.802
not being good enough at that period.

00:08:34.802 --> 00:08:37.630
But right now, we're totally different.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:40.214
Okay so what's helped
me is to realize that

00:08:40.214 --> 00:08:42.181
whatever's happened has happened.

00:08:42.181 --> 00:08:46.114
My only concern right now is where am I?

00:08:46.114 --> 00:08:47.935
I'm in nature, baby.

00:08:47.935 --> 00:08:51.056
And there is only right now.

00:08:51.056 --> 00:08:54.014
- That I think the best method

00:08:54.014 --> 00:08:57.681
to avoid fear or regret
at the time of death

00:08:58.727 --> 00:09:00.560
is while we are alive.

00:09:01.848 --> 00:09:05.931
Our time, our energy must
utilize meaningful way.

00:09:09.293 --> 00:09:12.043
Serving of that, that's like most

00:09:14.136 --> 00:09:16.184
(speaking in foreign language)

00:09:16.184 --> 00:09:18.684
way of, meaning of usefulness.

00:09:22.426 --> 00:09:26.009
Monsoon survivor, even
animals also can do.

00:09:31.254 --> 00:09:33.885
But for service to other

00:09:33.885 --> 00:09:37.052
is something unique about human being.

00:09:38.582 --> 00:09:41.752
I think (speaking foreign language)

00:09:41.752 --> 00:09:45.425
the mother and child or offspring--

00:09:45.425 --> 00:09:47.002
- [Translator] The bond.

00:09:47.002 --> 00:09:49.212
The bond between mother--
- Bond.

00:09:49.212 --> 00:09:51.629
Even other animals also have.

00:09:52.674 --> 00:09:57.193
But that kind of closer
feeling should be it.

00:09:57.193 --> 00:10:00.574
But we, human being,
because of intelligence,

00:10:00.574 --> 00:10:03.922
that kind of feeling we
can prolong, hold our life.

00:10:03.922 --> 00:10:06.409
- [Translator] Yeah,
extend it through our life.

00:10:06.409 --> 00:10:09.367
- So, serving other people.

00:10:09.367 --> 00:10:11.529
Helping other people.

00:10:11.529 --> 00:10:15.788
It's the, I think, very very
appropriate sort of action

00:10:15.788 --> 00:10:18.031
according our intelligence

00:10:18.031 --> 00:10:19.786
of human ability.

00:10:19.786 --> 00:10:21.899
We have special ability.

00:10:21.899 --> 00:10:26.028
So to utilize that ability
(speaking in foreign language).

00:10:26.028 --> 00:10:27.360
- [Translator] The most appropriate way.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.595
- Oh, most appropriate way
is serving other people.

00:10:30.595 --> 00:10:33.595
Then at the end, you feel no regret.

00:10:35.666 --> 00:10:39.833
I done my best, some useful
sort of meaningful life.

00:10:42.151 --> 00:10:46.068
Now I come, although
sorry, sad, but no regret.

00:10:47.109 --> 00:10:48.815
- So I'm with Jeff Bezos on this one,

00:10:48.815 --> 00:10:51.399
I think the best way to live
your life without regrets

00:10:51.399 --> 00:10:54.569
is to imagine yourself on your deathbed

00:10:54.569 --> 00:10:57.478
looking back at your life
and looking at the situation

00:10:57.478 --> 00:10:59.933
that you're in front of right
now and asking yourself,

00:10:59.933 --> 00:11:02.224
am I going to regret not doing this?

00:11:02.224 --> 00:11:04.402
Am I going to regret saying no?

00:11:04.402 --> 00:11:06.360
Am I going to regret being afraid?

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:08.384
Because if you are then
you know you have to go out

00:11:08.384 --> 00:11:09.408
and do it.

00:11:09.408 --> 00:11:10.871
For me, that's what saved me.

00:11:10.871 --> 00:11:13.081
Whenever I'm in a situation
that I'm afraid of doing,

00:11:13.081 --> 00:11:14.837
it's not don't be afraid.

00:11:14.837 --> 00:11:17.145
'Cause I'll be afraid,
it's okay to be afraid.

00:11:17.145 --> 00:11:19.404
But the thing that gets
me through the fear

00:11:19.404 --> 00:11:23.906
is that bigger fear of regretting
it later on down the line.

00:11:23.906 --> 00:11:26.377
And being able to make that
mental leap inside your head

00:11:26.377 --> 00:11:28.929
to understand the short
term thing you're feeling

00:11:28.929 --> 00:11:32.326
is fear and you don't just
disguise it with a reason.

00:11:32.326 --> 00:11:34.081
'Cause there's always
a practical reason why

00:11:34.081 --> 00:11:35.365
you shouldn't do something.

00:11:35.365 --> 00:11:37.706
There's always a logical
reason why you shouldn't do it,

00:11:37.706 --> 00:11:39.250
and if you can get through that

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.542
to understand that that's
not actually the real reason

00:11:41.542 --> 00:11:44.289
why I'm not doing it, I
can deal with those things,

00:11:44.289 --> 00:11:45.801
I could fix those problems.

00:11:45.801 --> 00:11:48.222
The real reason is I'm just afraid.

00:11:48.222 --> 00:11:51.392
And then if you think about
your life at the end of the road

00:11:51.392 --> 00:11:54.276
looking back on it, for
me the best way to do it

00:11:54.276 --> 00:11:56.252
is to work on building that muscle.

00:11:56.252 --> 00:11:58.657
For anytime you're afraid
of doing something,

00:11:58.657 --> 00:12:00.445
start building the muscle.

00:12:00.445 --> 00:12:02.412
At the start you're
going to be really weak,

00:12:02.412 --> 00:12:03.245
just like anything else.

00:12:03.245 --> 00:12:04.785
When you start lifting
any kind of weights,

00:12:04.785 --> 00:12:05.793
you're really really weak.

00:12:05.793 --> 00:12:08.832
But as soon as you find yourself
being afraid of something,

00:12:08.832 --> 00:12:12.132
try to train yourself to push through it.

00:12:12.132 --> 00:12:13.969
And so I've told the story about

00:12:13.969 --> 00:12:15.724
when I was wearing different colored socks

00:12:15.724 --> 00:12:17.918
because my son Hayden, seven years old,

00:12:17.918 --> 00:12:20.243
was wearing different
colored socks, always has to.

00:12:20.243 --> 00:12:23.120
And so I wanted to one day
wear different colored socks,

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:26.679
but I was afraid of what
other people would think.

00:12:26.679 --> 00:12:28.678
And as soon as I recognized
I was only not doing it

00:12:28.678 --> 00:12:30.434
because I was afraid of
what people would think,

00:12:30.434 --> 00:12:31.767
then I had to go out and do it.

00:12:31.767 --> 00:12:33.148
I had to build that muscle.

00:12:33.148 --> 00:12:34.481
Or the time when I'm
walking down the street

00:12:34.481 --> 00:12:37.894
and I'm dancing and grooving
'cause I got songs in my ear.

00:12:37.894 --> 00:12:39.487
And I love it and I'm vibing.

00:12:39.487 --> 00:12:41.763
And as I get closer to
a main intersection,

00:12:41.763 --> 00:12:44.038
I shrink down and I'm just doing this

00:12:44.038 --> 00:12:45.989
because now all of a sudden
there's people around.

00:12:45.989 --> 00:12:50.101
And most of the time we shrink
down without even noticing.

00:12:50.101 --> 00:12:53.791
It's so subconscious, it's
so natural to shrink down.

00:12:53.791 --> 00:12:56.001
It's so natural to play the smaller game

00:12:56.001 --> 00:12:58.179
because you're concerned
about what other people think.

00:12:58.179 --> 00:12:59.935
And as soon as I caught myself saying

00:12:59.935 --> 00:13:03.283
wait why am I playing
the smaller game here,

00:13:03.283 --> 00:13:04.697
why am I so afraid?

00:13:04.697 --> 00:13:05.921
Why am I concerned about
what are these people

00:13:05.921 --> 00:13:08.501
going to think if I'm
bustin' out some dance moves?

00:13:08.501 --> 00:13:11.134
So as soon as I recognized
I was holding myself back

00:13:11.134 --> 00:13:13.637
because of the fear of
other people's judgments,

00:13:13.637 --> 00:13:16.205
then I had to go and dance bigger.

00:13:16.205 --> 00:13:19.245
I had to go and groove
it out on the street.

00:13:19.245 --> 00:13:20.078
And dance.

00:13:20.078 --> 00:13:21.244
And build the muscle.

00:13:21.244 --> 00:13:23.389
And so anytime you catch yourself

00:13:23.389 --> 00:13:25.974
doing something and the only
reason is because you're

00:13:25.974 --> 00:13:29.355
afraid of it, work on
building that muscle.

00:13:29.355 --> 00:13:31.906
Because the last thing
I want for any of you

00:13:31.906 --> 00:13:33.646
and the last thing I want for myself

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:36.523
and the people around me
is to be on my deathbed,

00:13:36.523 --> 00:13:39.399
however old that's going to
be, looking back on my life,

00:13:39.399 --> 00:13:42.520
looking back on this moment and regretting

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:45.937
that I played small because I was afraid.

00:13:47.965 --> 00:13:49.465
Build your muscle.

00:13:51.915 --> 00:13:53.183
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:53.183 --> 00:13:55.605
I made this video because
Ghita asked me to.

00:13:55.605 --> 00:13:57.100
So if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.197
in the next edition of Believe Life,

00:13:59.197 --> 00:14:00.530
leave it down in the comments below

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:01.667
and I'll see what I can do.

00:14:01.667 --> 00:14:04.236
I'd love to know what did
you think of this video.

00:14:04.236 --> 00:14:06.202
What was the clip that
inspired you the most,

00:14:06.202 --> 00:14:07.909
what did you learn from
this that you're going to

00:14:07.909 --> 00:14:10.705
immediately apply somehow to
your life or to your business?

00:14:10.705 --> 00:14:12.070
Leave it in the comments below,

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:13.647
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:14:13.647 --> 00:14:16.068
I'd also love to know how do
you live life without regrets?

00:14:16.068 --> 00:14:18.409
What are some of your strategies
that maybe haven't been

00:14:18.409 --> 00:14:20.246
covered in this video yet
that you want to share

00:14:20.246 --> 00:14:21.952
that may help Believe Nation

00:14:21.952 --> 00:14:23.253
and the people watching as well.

00:14:23.253 --> 00:14:26.617
Leave it down in the comments
and do a good public service.

00:14:26.617 --> 00:14:27.788
Finally I wanted to give a quick shout out

00:14:27.788 --> 00:14:28.747
to Thelma Saunders.

00:14:28.747 --> 00:14:31.201
Thelma, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:14:31.201 --> 00:14:34.078
Your One Word, and posting
it to Twitter as well.

00:14:34.078 --> 00:14:35.915
I really really appreciate the support.

00:14:35.915 --> 00:14:37.377
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:37.377 --> 00:14:38.336
I believe in you.

00:14:38.336 --> 00:14:40.417
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:14:40.417 --> 00:14:42.497
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:42.497 --> 00:14:46.664
Much love, have an amazing
day and I'll see you soon.

00:14:52.136 --> 00:14:55.376
- I don't think I would change anything.

00:14:55.376 --> 00:14:57.337
Because I think it's
important to go through life

00:14:57.337 --> 00:14:59.004
without any regrets.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.758
People have said to me,

00:15:01.758 --> 00:15:05.676
would you change '98, would
you change the red card

00:15:05.676 --> 00:15:07.301
against Argentina?

00:15:07.301 --> 00:15:09.804
Do I wish it hadn't have happened?

00:15:09.804 --> 00:15:11.169
Of course.

00:15:11.169 --> 00:15:13.851
But if it hadn't have
happened, would I have been

00:15:13.851 --> 00:15:15.851
the player that I am today,

00:15:15.851 --> 00:15:19.443
would I have been the
strong person on the field

00:15:19.443 --> 00:15:22.092
and off the field that I am today?

00:15:22.092 --> 00:15:25.944
So there's nothing, nothing I regret.

00:15:25.944 --> 00:15:28.187
- Everything happens for a reason.

00:15:28.187 --> 00:15:30.430
How many times have people told you that

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:32.153
and it's really annoying right now?

00:15:32.153 --> 00:15:33.567
Don't tell me that.

00:15:33.567 --> 00:15:35.029
Now why do people say this?

00:15:35.029 --> 00:15:38.101
Because subconsciously,
we know it's the truth.

00:15:38.101 --> 00:15:40.019
What helped me along
my journey was to start

00:15:40.019 --> 00:15:41.596
connecting the dots.

00:15:41.596 --> 00:15:45.346
I now realize everything
that I went through,

00:15:47.691 --> 00:15:49.691
everything I've gone through,

00:15:49.691 --> 00:15:52.356
has led me up to where I am today.

00:15:52.356 --> 00:15:54.989
I got to thank those shoddy jobs.

00:15:54.989 --> 00:15:57.444
My irresponsible behavior.

00:15:57.444 --> 00:16:00.646
And it's going to continue to
be very irresponsible right?

00:16:00.646 --> 00:16:03.783
It's going to continue
to be very irresponsible.

00:16:03.783 --> 00:16:07.099
There are no saints here, baby.

00:16:07.099 --> 00:16:09.049
This ain't the Brady Bunch.

00:16:09.049 --> 00:16:10.349
Okay?

00:16:10.349 --> 00:16:11.893
So you got to have a sense of humor,

00:16:11.893 --> 00:16:14.104
you got to realize that okay,

00:16:14.104 --> 00:16:17.143
everything you are going
through is preparing you

00:16:17.143 --> 00:16:18.899
for the next step.

00:16:18.899 --> 00:16:23.856
It's what I call coming off
your righteous high horse.

00:16:23.856 --> 00:16:26.181
Now I share a lot.

00:16:26.181 --> 00:16:27.644
And it's very introspective,

00:16:27.644 --> 00:16:29.269
that why I always say
this is what's helped me

00:16:29.269 --> 00:16:30.686
along my journey.

00:16:31.878 --> 00:16:36.045
Everybody has to realize
nobody has it all figured out.

00:16:37.899 --> 00:16:40.743
Even though I'm a psychologist.

00:16:40.743 --> 00:16:42.326
I inspire millions.

00:16:43.815 --> 00:16:45.398
I'm still evolving.

00:16:46.351 --> 00:16:49.131
But I realize if I can realize that

00:16:49.131 --> 00:16:50.691
it's okay.

00:16:50.691 --> 00:16:53.779
The past is okay, even
if it's really grimy.

00:16:53.779 --> 00:16:57.946
Even if you want to put a
blindfold on, that's fine.

00:16:58.948 --> 00:17:02.426
But realize, that was meant to happen.

00:17:02.426 --> 00:17:04.113
Why? Because it did.

00:17:04.113 --> 00:17:08.420
There are no accidents or
coincidences in this universe.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:12.044
Everything is in divine
order, I accept that,

00:17:12.044 --> 00:17:15.247
I'm not in resistance to that.

00:17:15.247 --> 00:17:17.347
Powerful mantra, right there.

